module-description = Automatic moderation: rules that check every message, and act on the first one that hits.
config-automod-dry_run = Act on nothing: post what would have happened to the log channel.
config-automod-warn_expire_days = After how many days a warning of a rule expires.
config-automod-dm_on_action = Whether the member gets a direct message about a punishment.
config-automod-timeout_method = How a timeout is given: Discord's timeout, or a role that is taken off when its time is up.
config-automod-timeout_role = The id of the role a timeout gives, when timeout_method is role.
config-automod-counters = The counters, keyed by name: the numbers the rules add to, set, and react to.
config-automod-rules = The rules, keyed by id. Each one is checked on every message; the rules are checked in the order of their ids, and the first one that trips acts unless it says to continue.
config-automod-antiraid = Antiraid: the levels a server is raised to while a raid runs. Absent means antiraid is off.
config-automod-levels = The levels, the first being the calm one. Defaults to none, low, medium, high, lockdown.
config-automod-effects = What each level does, keyed by level name. A level without an entry does nothing.
config-automod-quarantine_release = Reserved: a quarantine is released by a moderator, never by a level going down.
config-automod-channels = The channels to slow down. Empty means every text channel of the server.
config-automod-pause_invites = Whether new invites are switched off while the level lasts.
config-automod-role = A role of the server. Absent means a role Closure creates.
config-automod-notify_channel = A channel that is told when the level changes.
config-automod-name = The name shown in logs. Defaults to the id.
config-automod-triggers = Any one of them tripping trips the rule.
config-automod-actions = Run in order.
config-automod-cooldown = After the rule fired for a member, it is skipped for that member for this long.
config-automod-continue_after_match = Whether the rules after this one still run when it trips.
command-automod = automod
    .description = Automatic moderation: its rules and state
subcommand-automod-status = status
    .description = Show whether dry run is on and which rules run

status-title = Automod status
status-dry-run = Dry run: { $state }
state-on = on
state-off = off
status-counts = Rules: { $enabled } enabled, { $disabled } disabled, { $invalid } invalid.
status-none = No rules are set.
status-rule = - `{ $id }` ({ $name }): triggers { $triggers }. Actions: { $actions }.{ $cooldown }
status-rule-off = - `{ $id }` ({ $name }), disabled: triggers { $triggers }. Actions: { $actions }.{ $cooldown }
status-cooldown = Cooldown: { $time }.
status-invalid-heading = Invalid rules (they never run):
status-invalid = - `{ $label }`: { $reason }

problem-shape = The rule does not have the shape the schema describes: { $error }
problem-id = The id is 1 to 32 characters: lowercase letters, digits, _ and -.
problem-name = The name is 1 to 64 characters.
problem-triggers = A rule has 1 to 20 triggers.
problem-actions = A rule has 1 to 12 actions.
problem-too-many = At most 100 rules are read.
problem-member-age = The member age needs min_days not above max_days, and at most 36500 days.
problem-cooldown = A cooldown is at least one second and at most 30 days.
problem-words = A words trigger has 1 to 500 words of 1 to 100 characters, and at least one target.
problem-patterns = A regex trigger has 1 to 20 patterns.
problem-pattern = A pattern is 1 to 200 characters.
problem-regex = A pattern does not compile, or is too big.
problem-domains = A links trigger has at most 200 domains and 50 regexes of each kind, none of them empty.
problem-invites = An invites trigger has at most 100 codes of each kind, none of them empty.
problem-attachments = An attachments trigger needs a count or a list of extensions or types, within the limits.
problem-caps = Caps need max_ratio from 0 to 1 and min_letters from 1 to 2000.
problem-repeat = Repeat max_run is 2 to 2000.
problem-stickers = Stickers max is 0 to 10.
problem-amount = A spam amount is 1 to 10000.
problem-window = A spam window is at least one second and at most one hour. Per channel, distinct channels and duplicates need one.
problem-distinct = Distinct channels is 2 to 50.
problem-purge = A purge looks back at least one second and at most seven days.
problem-timeout = A timeout lasts at least one second and at most 28 days.
problem-duration = A duration is readable, such as 1h, 30m or 7d, and not zero.
problem-delete-days = Delete days are 0 to 7.
problem-text = A reply text is 1 to 2000 characters.
problem-auto-delete = A reply's auto_delete is at least one second and at most seven days.
problem-template = A text template does not parse: check the braces.

